# 05 — Testing and Performance

## 1. Test Strategy

The viewport is the hardest module to test because of WebGL dependencies. Tests are split into three tiers:

| Tier | What | How | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Unit** | Render model builders, adapters, store logic, resource tracker | Vitest, no WebGL | Every PR |
| **Integration** | Dirty loop scheduling, resource hook → adapter → render model flow | Vitest with mocked canvas | Every PR |
| **Memory stress** | Resource leaks across 3D↔2D switches, quantity cycles | Vitest with tracked disposal counts | Weekly / pre-release |

## 2. Required Unit Tests

### Domain Adapters
- `FdmDomainAdapter` builds correct cell-center positions from grid metadata
- `FemDomainAdapter` produces correct positions, indices, normals from decoded topology
- `createDomainAdapter` selects correct adapter class
- Adapter caches positions (second call returns same reference)

### Render Model Builder
- `buildViewport3DRenderModel` produces null topology when adapter is null
- Topology revision matches adapter generationId
- Scalar field mapped correctly from field resource
- Layer visibility flags propagated
- Selection data mapped from kernel selection state

### WebGL Resource Tracker
- `track` + `releaseCategory` disposes all in category
- `releaseAll` disposes everything
- `getCounts` reflects actual registrations
- Double-dispose doesn't throw

### Viewport Store
- Grid layout switch produces correct pane configs
- Active pane change updates state
- Display mode change per pane
- Camera linking toggle
- Maximise/restore toggles correctly

## 3. Required Integration Tests

### Dirty Render Loop
```typescript
test("no frame rendered when nothing is dirty", () => {
  const loop = createDirtyRenderLoop(mockScene, mockModel);
  advanceTimers(1000);
  expect(mockScene.render).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
});

test("one frame after markDirty(camera)", () => {
  const loop = createDirtyRenderLoop(mockScene, mockModel);
  loop.markDirty("camera");
  advanceToNextFrame();
  expect(mockScene.render).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
});

test("multiple dirty marks coalesce to one frame", () => {
  const loop = createDirtyRenderLoop(mockScene, mockModel);
  loop.markDirty("camera");
  loop.markDirty("field");
  loop.markDirty("selection");
  advanceToNextFrame();
  expect(mockScene.render).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
});
```

### Quantity Switch Without Topology Rebuild
```typescript
test("quantity switch updates field but not topology", () => {
  const adapter = new FdmDomainAdapter(mockMeta);
  const model1 = buildRenderModel(adapter, fieldA, viz);
  const model2 = buildRenderModel(adapter, fieldB, viz);

  expect(model1.topology!.topologyRevision).toBe(model2.topology!.topologyRevision);
  expect(model1.scalarField!.quantityId).not.toBe(model2.scalarField!.quantityId);
});
```

### Selection Does Not Refetch Field
```typescript
test("selection change does not trigger field resource fetch", () => {
  // Mount viewport, load data
  // Change selection
  // Assert field hook did not refetch
});
```

## 4. Memory Stress Test

Procedure (automated in Vitest):

```
1. Mount viewport-3d module
2. Load FDM domain + field
3. Assert tracker.getCounts() > 0
4. Switch quantity 5 times
5. Assert tracker.getCounts() stays bounded (no growth per switch)
6. Switch to viewport-2d module
7. Assert 3D tracker.getCounts() === all zeros (3D resources released)
8. Switch back to viewport-3d
9. Assert tracker.getCounts() > 0 again (rebuilt)
10. Switch grid layout: single → quad → single
11. Assert tracker.getCounts() bounded
12. Unmount viewport-3d
13. Assert tracker.getCounts() === all zeros
```

## 5. Idle Performance Audit

Automated test:

```
1. Mount viewport with data loaded
2. Wait for initial settling (all dirty reasons processed)
3. Start frame counter
4. Wait 5 seconds
5. Assert frame count === 0
6. Assert no requestAnimationFrame active
7. Assert no setInterval active
8. Assert no fetch requests in progress
```

## 6. Context Loss Recovery Test

```
1. Mount viewport, render initial frame
2. Simulate webglcontextlost event
3. Assert no render attempts during lost state
4. Simulate webglcontextrestored event
5. Assert one frame rendered
6. Assert tracker.getCounts() matches initial (no leaks from lost resources)
```

## 7. Performance Budgets

| Metric | Budget |
|---|---|
| Initial render (first frame after data load) | < 100ms |
| Quantity switch (field buffer swap) | < 50ms |
| Topology rebuild (new mesh) | < 200ms for 1M cells |
| Camera orbit (interactive frame) | < 16ms (60fps) |
| Idle frame count (per minute) | 0 |
| Memory growth per quantity switch | < 1MB |
| Memory growth per 3D↔2D switch | 0 (net, after GC) |

## 8. Diagnostics Surface

The viewport module exposes diagnostic data to the `diagnostics` module:

```typescript
export interface ViewportDiagnostics {
  frameCount: number;
  lastFrameDirtyReasons: DirtyReason[];
  fps: number;
  resourceCounts: Record<string, number>;
  activeAnimationFrames: number;
  topologyRevision: number | null;
  fieldRevision: number | null;
  paneCount: number;
  activeDisplayModes: DisplayMode[];
}
```

Visible in the diagnostics panel in development mode. Not shipped to production.

## 9. Verification Commands

```bash
# Unit + integration tests
pnpm --dir apps/control-room test -- --run viewport

# Memory stress
pnpm --dir apps/control-room test -- --run viewport-memory-stress

# Idle audit
pnpm --dir apps/control-room audit:idle-performance

# Typecheck + lint (zero-tolerance gate)
pnpm --dir apps/control-room typecheck
pnpm --dir apps/control-room lint
```
